IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`
IMPORT `er4-part3-reg63-weekly-indemnity-plan`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), PART III, "Standards", regs 64, 65 and 66: the requirements that a
-- Special Weekly Indemnity Plan, a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan and an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave plan
-- must meet. Layer 1 (the law, objectively), piece er4. Unofficial plain-text rendering; nothing here is "verified
-- against the official text". No section GIVEN: every rule has its own GIVEN.
--
-- THE SHAPE. 64(b) and 65(a) each "satisfy all the requirements of section 63, except the requirements of
-- paragraphs 63(e) and (f)": the record of each CONTAINS the reg 63 case and the rule calls the paragraph rules of
-- module er4-part3-reg63-weekly-indemnity-plan for (a), (b), (c), (d) and (g). 66(a) takes over 65 "except 65(b),
-- 65(c)(i), 65(e) and (f)": the record of 66 contains the 65 case, and 66(a) calls 65(a) and 65(d) (65(c)(ii) and (iii)
-- are permissions, not requirements, so there is nothing in them to satisfy; fork F8).
-- Paragraphs 65(c) and 66(c) say what a plan MAY do "notwithstanding paragraph (b)". They are encoded as the three
-- things they permit, each as a small rule, and they add nothing to the tests the plan must pass.

§ `Regulation 64 -- Special Weekly Indemnity Plan`

-- src:1075 | (a) the plan must be provided or financed, in whole or in part, by an employer that is Her Majesty in right of a province, a provincial Crown corporation, a municipal authority or a public authority of a province or an institution primarily controlled, supported or financed by a province;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 64(a) (src:1075)
DECLARE `er4 Employer that provides or finances a plan` IS ONE OF
    `er4 Her Majesty in right of a province`
    `er4 a provincial Crown corporation`
    `er4 a municipal authority`
    `er4 a public authority of a province`
    `er4 an institution primarily controlled, supported or financed by a province`
    `er4 any other employer`

-- src:1074 | 64 A Special Weekly Indemnity Plan shall meet the following requirements:
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 64 (src:1074)
DECLARE `er4 Case under a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan` HAS
    `er4 section 63 case of the special plan`                                       IS A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`   -- 64(b)
    `er4 employer that provides or finances the special plan`                       IS A `er4 Employer that provides or finances a plan`   -- 64(a)
    `er4 active employment after which full benefits are reinstated under the special plan, in months`   IS A NUMBER   -- 64(c)
    `er4 longest period for which the special plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in weeks`    IS A NUMBER   -- 64(d)(i)
    `er4 events that end payment of benefits under the special plan`                IS A LIST OF `er4 Event that ends payment of benefits under a plan`   -- 64(d)

-- src:1075 | (a) the plan must be provided or financed, in whole or in part, by an employer that is Her Majesty in right of a province, a provincial Crown corporation, a municipal authority or a public authority of a province or an institution primarily controlled, supported or financed by a province;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 64(a) (src:1075)
GIVEN s IS A `er4 Case under a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 64(a) the plan is provided or financed, in whole or in part, by an employer the paragraph names` s IF
    CONSIDER s's `er4 employer that provides or finances the special plan`
    WHEN `er4 any other employer` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:1076 | (b) the plan must satisfy all the requirements of section 63, except the requirements of paragraphs 63(e) and (f);
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 64(b) (src:1076)
GIVEN s IS A `er4 Case under a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 64(b) the plan satisfies all the requirements of section 63 except paragraphs 63(e) and (f)` s IF
        `reg 63(a) the person becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan in time` (s's `er4 section 63 case of the special plan`)
    AND `reg 63(b) any elimination period does not exceed seven consecutive days beginning with the first day of the period of incapacity` (s's `er4 section 63 case of the special plan`)
    AND `reg 63(c) benefits are paid in full regardless of the benefits payable under the Act and from other sources` (s's `er4 section 63 case of the special plan`)
    AND `reg 63(d) the benefits payable under the plan are at least 55% of the normal weekly insurable earnings` (s's `er4 section 63 case of the special plan`)
    AND `reg 63(g) the only conditions precluding payment are conditions the paragraph lists` (s's `er4 section 63 case of the special plan`)

-- src:1077 | (c) subject to the elimination period referred to in paragraph 63(b), full benefits payable under the plan to an insured person are reinstated after one month of active employment following their most recent absence due to illness or injury; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 64(c) (src:1077)
GIVEN s IS A `er4 Case under a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 64(c) full benefits are reinstated after one month of active employment` s IF
    s's `er4 active employment after which full benefits are reinstated under the special plan, in months` AT MOST 1

-- src:1078 | (d) in any case not referred to in paragraph (c) and subject to the elimination period referred to in paragraph 63(b), benefits under the plan are payable with respect to the insured person's illness or injury until the earliest of
-- src:1079 | (i) the end of a period of at least 52 weeks during which the benefits are paid,
-- src:1080 | (ii) the end of the period of incapacity due to the illness or injury,
-- src:1081 | (iii) the date the insured person retires, and
-- src:1082 | (iv) the date of the insured person's separation from employment resulting from any reason other than illness or injury, where notice of the separation was given before the onset of the illness or the occurrence of the injury.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 64(d) (src:1078-1082)
GIVEN event IS A `er4 Event that ends payment of benefits under a plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 64(d) an event at which payment under the plan may end` event IF
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN `er4 the end of a period during which the benefits are paid` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er4 the end of the period of incapacity due to the illness or injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er4 the date the insured person retires` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er4 the date of the insured person's separation from employment for a reason other than illness or injury, notice having been given before the onset of the illness or the occurrence of the injury` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 64(d) (src:1078-1082)
GIVEN s IS A `er4 Case under a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 64(d) benefits are payable until the earliest of the four events` s IF
        s's `er4 longest period for which the special plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in weeks` AT LEAST 52
    AND all `reg 64(d) an event at which payment under the plan may end` (s's `er4 events that end payment of benefits under the special plan`)

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 64 (src:1074-1082)
GIVEN s IS A `er4 Case under a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 64 the plan meets the requirements of a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan` s IF
        `reg 64(a) the plan is provided or financed, in whole or in part, by an employer the paragraph names` s
    AND `reg 64(b) the plan satisfies all the requirements of section 63 except paragraphs 63(e) and (f)` s
    AND `reg 64(c) full benefits are reinstated after one month of active employment` s
    AND `reg 64(d) benefits are payable until the earliest of the four events` s

§ `Regulation 65 -- Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`

-- src:1083 | 65 A Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan shall meet the following requirements:
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 65 (src:1083)
DECLARE `er4 Case under a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` HAS
    `er4 section 63 case of the cumulative plan`                                    IS A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`   -- 65(a)
    `er4 cumulative plan credits only after the period or the hours referred to in paragraph 63(a)`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- 65(b)
    `er4 days of paid sick leave credited by the cumulative plan for each subsequent full month of active employment`   IS A NUMBER   -- 65(b)
    `er4 days each month that the cumulative plan makes available only for illness or injury, pregnancy, child care or care or support of a family member`   IS A NUMBER   -- 65(b)
    `er4 months for which the cumulative plan defers eligibility to use paid sick leave`   IS A NUMBER   -- 65(d); 0 if eligibility is not deferred
    `er4 cumulative plan accumulates unused days at the rate in paragraphs 65(b) and (c)`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- 65(e)
    `er4 maximum working days of paid sick leave the cumulative plan lets a person accumulate`   IS A NUMBER   -- 65(e)
    `er4 longest period for which the cumulative plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in working days`   IS A NUMBER   -- 65(f)(i)
    `er4 events that end payment of benefits under the cumulative plan`             IS A LIST OF `er4 Event that ends payment of benefits under a plan`   -- 65(f)

-- src:1084 | (a) the plan must satisfy all the requirements of section 63, except the requirements of paragraphs 63(e) and (f);
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 65(a) (src:1084)
GIVEN p IS A `er4 Case under a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 65(a) the plan satisfies all the requirements of section 63 except paragraphs 63(e) and (f)` p IF
        `reg 63(a) the person becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan in time` (p's `er4 section 63 case of the cumulative plan`)
    AND `reg 63(b) any elimination period does not exceed seven consecutive days beginning with the first day of the period of incapacity` (p's `er4 section 63 case of the cumulative plan`)
    AND `reg 63(c) benefits are paid in full regardless of the benefits payable under the Act and from other sources` (p's `er4 section 63 case of the cumulative plan`)
    AND `reg 63(d) the benefits payable under the plan are at least 55% of the normal weekly insurable earnings` (p's `er4 section 63 case of the cumulative plan`)
    AND `reg 63(g) the only conditions precluding payment are conditions the paragraph lists` (p's `er4 section 63 case of the cumulative plan`)

-- "One or more days ... for each subsequent full month of active employment, of which at least one day per month is
-- available only for the insured person's illness or injury, while at home because of pregnancy or to care for a
-- child ... or while providing care or support" is read as: at least one day credited each full month, and at least
-- one of them reserved for those purposes (fork F9).
-- src:1085 | (b) the plan must credit an insured person covered by the plan, after the completion of the period referred to in subparagraph 63(a)(i) or after the accumulation of the number of hours referred to in subparagraph 63(a)(ii), with one or more days of paid sick leave for each subsequent full month of active employment, of which at least one day per month is available only for the insured person’s illness or injury, while the insured person remains at home because of pregnancy or to care for a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Act or while the insured person is providing care or support to a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) of the Act, to a critically ill child or to a critically ill adult;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 65(b) (src:1085)
GIVEN p IS A `er4 Case under a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 65(b) the plan credits at least one day of paid sick leave each full month, at least one of them reserved` p IF
        p's `er4 cumulative plan credits only after the period or the hours referred to in paragraph 63(a)`
    AND p's `er4 days of paid sick leave credited by the cumulative plan for each subsequent full month of active employment` AT LEAST 1
    AND p's `er4 days each month that the cumulative plan makes available only for illness or injury, pregnancy, child care or care or support of a family member` AT LEAST 1

§§ `Regulation 65(c) -- what the plan may do notwithstanding paragraph (b)`

-- src:1086 | (c) notwithstanding paragraph (b), the plan may
-- src:1087 | (i) allow the paid sick leave credit referred to in that paragraph to be prorated in relation to the total period of active employment in a month,
-- "Prorated in relation to the total period of active employment in a month": the credit for a full month times the
-- part of a full month's active employment that the person actually worked (fork F10). A full month of nothing
-- (a period of zero or less) has no proportion: NOTHING.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 65(c)(i) (src:1086-1087)
GIVEN `the credit for a full month, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the active employment in the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the active employment in a full month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 65(c)(i) the paid sick leave credit for a month, prorated in relation to the active employment in the month` MEANS
    IF `the active employment in a full month` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the credit for a full month, in days` TIMES (`the active employment in the month` DIVIDED BY `the active employment in a full month`))

-- src:1088 | (ii) preclude the accumulation of paid sick leave for a month in which the insured person has not been actively employed for at least twice the number of hours in the insured person's normal work week, and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 65(c)(ii) (src:1088)
GIVEN `hours of active employment in the month` IS A NUMBER
      `hours in the person's normal work week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 65(c)(ii) the plan may preclude the accumulation of paid sick leave for the month` IF
    `hours of active employment in the month` LESS THAN (2 TIMES `hours in the person's normal work week`)

-- src:1089 | (iii) allow the insured person to use paid sick leave while remaining at home because of pregnancy or to care for a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Act or while providing care or support to a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) of the Act, to a critically ill child or to a critically ill adult.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 65(c)(iii) (src:1089)
DECLARE `er4 Purpose for which paid sick leave may be used while at home` IS ONE OF
    `er4 pregnancy`
    `er4 caring for a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Act`
    `er4 providing care or support to a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) of the Act`
    `er4 providing care or support to a critically ill child`
    `er4 providing care or support to a critically ill adult`
    `er4 another purpose`

-- The paragraph names five purposes; for any other the paragraph says nothing: NOTHING.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 65(c)(iii) (src:1089)
GIVEN purpose IS A `er4 Purpose for which paid sick leave may be used while at home`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 65(c)(iii) the plan may allow the insured person to use paid sick leave while remaining at home for` purpose MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `er4 another purpose` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "Eligibility to use paid sick leave is deferred" for a temporary or probationary person: not for more than 12
-- months from the day the person commences employment or joins the plan; no deferral at all is 0 months.
-- src:1090 | (d) where eligibility to use paid sick leave is deferred in the case of an insured person who is employed on a temporary basis or is serving a probationary period, it cannot be deferred for a period greater than 12 months beginning on the day the insured person commences employment or joins the plan;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 65(d) (src:1090)
GIVEN p IS A `er4 Case under a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 65(d) any deferral of eligibility to use paid sick leave is for no more than 12 months` p IF
    p's `er4 months for which the cumulative plan defers eligibility to use paid sick leave` AT MOST 12

-- src:1091 | (e) the days of paid sick leave available only in respect of the insured person’s illness or injury, or while the insured person remains at home because of pregnancy or to care for a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Act or while the insured person is providing care or support to a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) of the Act, to a critically ill child or to a critically ill adult, that are not used for those purposes must be accumulated at the rate prescribed in paragraphs (b) and (c), and the maximum number of days of paid sick leave that may be so accumulated is not less than 75 working days; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 65(e) (src:1091)
GIVEN p IS A `er4 Case under a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 65(e) unused days accumulate at the prescribed rate up to at least 75 working days` p IF
        p's `er4 cumulative plan accumulates unused days at the rate in paragraphs 65(b) and (c)`
    AND p's `er4 maximum working days of paid sick leave the cumulative plan lets a person accumulate` AT LEAST 75

-- src:1092 | (f) subject to the elimination period referred to in paragraph 63(b), benefits are payable under the plan with respect to the insured person's illness or injury until the earliest of
-- src:1093 | (i) the end of a period of at least 75 working days during which the benefits are paid,
-- src:1094 | (ii) the end of the period of incapacity due to the illness or injury,
-- src:1095 | (iii) the exhaustion of all accumulated paid sick leave,
-- src:1096 | (iv) the date the insured person retires, and
-- src:1097 | (v) the date of the insured person's separation from employment for any reason other than illness or injury, where notice of the separation was given before the onset of the illness or the occurrence of the injury.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 65(f) (src:1092-1097)
GIVEN event IS A `er4 Event that ends payment of benefits under a plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 65(f) an event at which payment under the plan may end` event IF
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN `er4 the end of a period during which the benefits are paid` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er4 the end of the period of incapacity due to the illness or injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er4 the exhaustion of all accumulated paid sick leave` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er4 the date the insured person retires` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er4 the date of the insured person's separation from employment for a reason other than illness or injury, notice having been given before the onset of the illness or the occurrence of the injury` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 65(f) (src:1092-1097)
GIVEN p IS A `er4 Case under a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 65(f) benefits are payable until the earliest of the five events` p IF
        p's `er4 longest period for which the cumulative plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in working days` AT LEAST 75
    AND all `reg 65(f) an event at which payment under the plan may end` (p's `er4 events that end payment of benefits under the cumulative plan`)

§§ `Regulation 65 -- all the requirements`

-- Paragraph (c) adds no test: it says what the plan may do. The requirements are (a), (b), (d), (e) and (f).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 65 (src:1083-1097)
GIVEN p IS A `er4 Case under a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 65 the plan meets the requirements of a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` p IF
        `reg 65(a) the plan satisfies all the requirements of section 63 except paragraphs 63(e) and (f)` p
    AND `reg 65(b) the plan credits at least one day of paid sick leave each full month, at least one of them reserved` p
    AND `reg 65(d) any deferral of eligibility to use paid sick leave is for no more than 12 months` p
    AND `reg 65(e) unused days accumulate at the prescribed rate up to at least 75 working days` p
    AND `reg 65(f) benefits are payable until the earliest of the five events` p

§ `Regulation 66 -- Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave plan`

-- src:1098 | 66 An Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave shall meet the following requirements:
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 66 (src:1098)
DECLARE `er4 Case under an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` HAS
    `er4 section 65 case of the enhanced plan`                                      IS A `er4 Case under a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`   -- 66(a)
    `er4 enhanced plan credits only after the period or the hours referred to in paragraph 63(a)`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- 66(b)
    `er4 days of paid sick leave credited by the enhanced plan for each subsequent full month of active employment`   IS A NUMBER   -- 66(b)
    `er4 days each month that the enhanced plan makes available only for illness or injury, pregnancy, child care or care or support of a family member`   IS A NUMBER   -- 66(b)
    `er4 enhanced plan accumulates unused days at the rate in paragraphs 66(b) and (c)`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- 66(d)
    `er4 maximum working days of paid sick leave the enhanced plan lets a person accumulate`   IS A NUMBER   -- 66(d)
    `er4 longest period for which the enhanced plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in working days`   IS A NUMBER   -- 66(e)(i)
    `er4 events that end payment of benefits under the enhanced plan`               IS A LIST OF `er4 Event that ends payment of benefits under a plan`   -- 66(e)

-- 66(a): all of section 65 except 65(b), 65(c)(i), 65(e) and 65(f): that leaves 65(a), 65(c)(ii) and (iii) (permissions,
-- nothing to satisfy) and 65(d).
-- src:1099 | (a) the plan must satisfy all the requirements of section 65, except the requirements of paragraph 65(b), subparagraph 65(c)(i) and paragraphs 65(e) and (f);
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 66(a) (src:1099)
GIVEN e IS A `er4 Case under an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(a) the plan satisfies all the requirements of section 65 except paragraph 65(b), subparagraph 65(c)(i) and paragraphs 65(e) and (f)` e IF
        `reg 65(a) the plan satisfies all the requirements of section 63 except paragraphs 63(e) and (f)` (e's `er4 section 65 case of the enhanced plan`)
    AND `reg 65(d) any deferral of eligibility to use paid sick leave is for no more than 12 months` (e's `er4 section 65 case of the enhanced plan`)

-- "One and two thirds or more days ... at least one and two thirds days per month" is 5/3 of a day.
-- src:1100 | (b) the plan must credit an insured person covered by the plan, after the completion of the period referred to in subparagraph 63(a)(i) or after the accumulation of the number of hours referred to in subparagraph 63(a)(ii), with one and two thirds or more days of paid sick leave for each subsequent full month of active employment, of which at least one and two thirds days per month are available only for the insured person’s illness or injury, while the insured person remains at home because of pregnancy or to care for a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Act or while the insured person is providing care or support to a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) of the Act, to a critically ill child or to a critically ill adult;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 66(b) (src:1100)
GIVEN e IS A `er4 Case under an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(b) the plan credits at least one and two thirds days of paid sick leave each full month, that many reserved` e IF
        e's `er4 enhanced plan credits only after the period or the hours referred to in paragraph 63(a)`
    AND e's `er4 days of paid sick leave credited by the enhanced plan for each subsequent full month of active employment` AT LEAST (5 DIVIDED BY 3)
    AND e's `er4 days each month that the enhanced plan makes available only for illness or injury, pregnancy, child care or care or support of a family member` AT LEAST (5 DIVIDED BY 3)

-- src:1101 | (c) notwithstanding paragraph (b), the plan may allow the paid sick leave credit referred to in that paragraph to be prorated in relation to the total period of active employment in a month;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 66(c) (src:1101)
GIVEN `the credit for a full month, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the active employment in the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the active employment in a full month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 66(c) the paid sick leave credit for a month, prorated in relation to the active employment in the month` MEANS
    IF `the active employment in a full month` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the credit for a full month, in days` TIMES (`the active employment in the month` DIVIDED BY `the active employment in a full month`))

-- src:1102 | (d) the days of paid sick leave available only in respect of the insured person’s illness or injury, while the insured person remains at home because of pregnancy or to care for a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Act, or while the insured person is providing care or support to a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) of the Act, to a critically ill child or to a critically ill adult, that are not used for those purposes, must be accumulated at the rate prescribed in paragraphs (b) and (c), and the maximum number of days of paid sick leave that may be so accumulated is not less than 125 working days; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 66(d) (src:1102)
GIVEN e IS A `er4 Case under an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(d) unused days accumulate at the prescribed rate up to at least 125 working days` e IF
        e's `er4 enhanced plan accumulates unused days at the rate in paragraphs 66(b) and (c)`
    AND e's `er4 maximum working days of paid sick leave the enhanced plan lets a person accumulate` AT LEAST 125

-- src:1103 | (e) subject to the elimination period referred to in paragraph 63(b), benefits are payable under the plan with respect to the insured person's illness or injury until the earliest of
-- src:1104 | (i) the end of a period of at least 125 working days during which the benefits are paid,
-- src:1105 | (ii) the end of the period of incapacity due to the illness or injury,
-- src:1106 | (iii) the exhaustion of all accumulated paid sick leave,
-- src:1107 | (iv) the date the insured person retires, and
-- src:1108 | (v) the date of the insured person's separation from employment for any reason other than illness or injury, where notice of the separation was given before the onset of the illness or the occurrence of the injury.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 66(e) (src:1103-1108)
GIVEN event IS A `er4 Event that ends payment of benefits under a plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(e) an event at which payment under the plan may end` event IF
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN `er4 the end of a period during which the benefits are paid` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er4 the end of the period of incapacity due to the illness or injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er4 the exhaustion of all accumulated paid sick leave` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er4 the date the insured person retires` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er4 the date of the insured person's separation from employment for a reason other than illness or injury, notice having been given before the onset of the illness or the occurrence of the injury` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 66(e) (src:1103-1108)
GIVEN e IS A `er4 Case under an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66(e) benefits are payable until the earliest of the five events` e IF
        e's `er4 longest period for which the enhanced plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in working days` AT LEAST 125
    AND all `reg 66(e) an event at which payment under the plan may end` (e's `er4 events that end payment of benefits under the enhanced plan`)

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 66 (src:1098-1108)
GIVEN e IS A `er4 Case under an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 66 the plan meets the requirements of an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave plan` e IF
        `reg 66(a) the plan satisfies all the requirements of section 65 except paragraph 65(b), subparagraph 65(c)(i) and paragraphs 65(e) and (f)` e
    AND `reg 66(b) the plan credits at least one and two thirds days of paid sick leave each full month, that many reserved` e
    AND `reg 66(d) unused days accumulate at the prescribed rate up to at least 125 working days` e
    AND `reg 66(e) benefits are payable until the earliest of the five events` e
